 ## Known limitations
 
+An unpackaged shell with `DSH_MARKET_ROOT` set to a local Market Agent checkout opens its `desktop/index.html` as the primary window. The Application menu switches between the market homepage and the normal dsh conversation. Only `index.html`, `style.css`, `renderer.js`, and `chart.js` are served from that checkout. The isolated preload exposes named monitor operations only on the main market page; Electron validates sender identity and top-level frame before reading `runtime/api-token` and contacting fixed loopback port 8765. Renderer code never receives the token. Packaged applications ignore this override; packaging the market service and assets requires separate release integration. The focused `apps/desktop/tests/market-home.spec.ts` suite checks the file allowlist, frame ownership and API input validation.
+
 - The Web "Open In..." action is disabled in Desktop because its host plugin requires HTTP routes; Desktop does not provide a `webServer`.
 - Release signing, notarization, update hosting, and previous-version installed-artifact qualification require the production release environment.
 - Desktop plugins with dependency lifecycle scripts are rejected unless their package appears in the desktop project's reviewed `allowBuilds` policy.
